{
  "manufacturer": "Vaisala",
  "manufacturer_slug": "vaisala",
  "model": "Origo10 transmitters for HVAC (Origo10A, Modbus RTU)",
  "model_slug": "origo10",
  "short_model": "Origo10",
  "aliases": [
    "Origo10",
    "Origo10A",
    "Origo 10",
    "Vaisala Origo10 duct transmitter",
    "Vaisala Origo10 wall transmitter"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Sensor (HVAC humidity, temperature and CO2 transmitter)",
  "applies_to": "Origo10A duct and wall transmitters ordered with the Modbus RTU output (user guide M213293EN-B). Origo10L has no Modbus.",
  "summary": "Origo10 is Vaisala's modular HVAC transmitter: a duct or wall housing that takes up to two probes (XMP10 humidity/temperature, CO2, temperature) and up to three plug-in modules such as the DIO10 relay/binary-input module. The Origo10A version offers Modbus RTU (or BACnet MS/TP) on RS-485. Each probe or module gets its own 4096-register block; this map lists probe A in full, the main probe B readings, module 1 relay/input, transmitter status, serial settings and test registers.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 240,
    "baud": 19200,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "1-based",
    "note": "Registers are numbered in decimal from 1 and the guide also prints the 0-based hex PDU address; register 1 is address 0x0000. Subdevice blocks: register = base + X * 4096, with X = 0 probe A, 1 probe B, 2-4 modules 1-3 (hex address 0xX000 style)."
  },
  "default_word_order": "CDAB",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Origo10 User Guide",
    "doc_number": "M213293EN-B",
    "revision_date": "2026-05",
    "url": "https://docs.vaisala.com/r/M213293EN-B/en-US",
    "pages": "Appendix A Modbus reference, pp. 125-134 (Tables 34-46)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "All registers are holding registers: read with function 03, write with function 16.",
    "32-bit floats and 32-bit integers/bitfields put the least significant word at the listed register (CDAB), as the guide states for both formats.",
    "Only probe A is listed in full. Probe B uses the same layout plus 4096 (e.g. RH at register 4353), and modules 1-3 add 8192, 12288 and 16384. Registers for parameters the fitted probe cannot measure are unavailable.",
    "Left out: the 16-bit integer copies of the measurements (897-910 + X*4096). The guide prints a 'scale factor' column (10, and 0.01 for CO2 ppm) but never says whether to multiply or divide the raw value by it, so the floats are listed instead. 0x8000 in an integer register means not available.",
    "Left out: most non-metric floats except RH, T, dew point and enthalpy, the remaining measurement-status registers (same bit layout), and the long identification strings (vendor URL, product name, manufacturing data).",
    "Modbus is only available on Origo10A transmitters. The protocol can be changed to BACnet MS/TP in Insight."
  ],
